From f5cc52cde33199298d854577594baa593586b35c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:31:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 104/116] DXF 3DSOLID: the SAT lines over 255 chars continued
 in 3

The SAT of the ACIS entities is written to DXF in 1 lines, and a line
over 255 chars continues in 3 lines. We wrote the encrypted blocks of
the DWG line by line, but these blocks of 4096 split the lines anywhere:
a line at the end of a block was written as two 1 lines, and the char
after it was dropped, so the numbers there broke (-0.8944579735636958 to
-0.89 and 44579735636958 in example_2000), lines over 255 were written
in one. And reading the DXF, the newline of a 1 line was put before its
3 continuation lines.

* src/out_dxf.c (dxf_sat_lines): New, the lines of all blocks, over 255
in 3, with "^ " for ^.
(dxf_3dsolid): Use it.
* src/in_dxf.c (add_3DSOLID_encr): The newline before a 1 line, not
after it, and at the end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
